summary.value:
The paper proposes RobuQ, a QAT framework for ultra-low-bit Transformer quantization, instantiated on DiT-XL/2. The method has three components: 

(i) RobustQuantizer—apply an all-layer Hadamard transform to “Gaussianize” per-token activations, then quantize with a per-token Gauss quantizer (uniform and Lloyd–Max); 

(ii) Activation-only Mixed-Precision (AMP)—fix weights to ternary (W1.58) and allocate per-layer activation bit-widths via a DP/knapsack objective; 

(iii) experiments on ImageNet-1K and FFHQ showing competitive A4/A3 and stable A2 under QAT.

